{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/700392-draco-a-potential-end-to-all-viral-disease-has-an-indigogo-campaign","id":700392,"title":"Draco, a potential end to all viral disease has an indigogo campaign.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-13T19:17:08-07:00","id":700392,"title":"Draco, a potential end to all viral disease has an indigogo campaign.","content":"<a href=\"https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/help-end-viral-diseases-with-dracos#/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/h...-with-dracos#/</a><br /> <br /> As I said in the title Draco is a potential cure for all viral based diseases like herpes, AIDS, ebola ect... which has had a successful proof of concept phase showing that Draco works on a verity of virus in human cells and in mice. But now they are in the valley of death, they've run out of money from the NIH and they need more research to show it works on more commerically profitible viral diseases so that they can get funding from new sources like pharma companies and governments.<br /> <br /> Just though people should know about this worthy campaign where they can help fund a eventual cure for all viral diseases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T19:30:44-07:00","id":700400,"title":"","content":"I'm concerned the pharmaceutical companies they're trying to reach would take it and bury it. They make much more money treating symptoms than actually curing illnesses. Sick people are repeat customers, healthy ones are not.<br /> <br /> That said, very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T21:26:12-07:00","id":700447,"title":"","content":"Sounds too good to be true. I am therefore doubtful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T11:08:23-07:00","id":701138,"title":"","content":"Man, this is something that would be awesome if it was true, but the sheer claim sounds so out there. I'm just not qualified to make a decision here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T14:05:04-07:00","id":701283,"title":"","content":"The ask is also... kinda of low. It adds to the suspicious nature of this project for me.<br /> <br /> I understand enough of the science to get why it's an appealing line of research to medicine, and something pharma might want buried.<br /> <br /> But there are lots of parties out there that would gladly cough up $100K for this if it was as big of a deal as it could be. The US military and Homeland Security consider highly infectious diseases like ebola major security issues. If you can cure ebola - as in we can said people to ebola infections in Africa without risk of them spreading it back here - they'd gladly shelve the production of a drone or whatever. They've got the budget.<br /> <br /> Even then... why aren't people like Bill Gates or the Clintons jumping on board through their charitable organizations? Again, the campaign is something they could easily toss cash at if they wanted to.<br /> <br /> I get the appeal of crowdfunding, and I get why the medical establishment can stagnate promising but out their research. But it seems really weird that they can't get $100K thrown at them through more traditional channels if this is even kind of possible.<br /> <br /> Edit: To put this in a bit of perspective, the Smithsonian kickstarter to make a space suit available to the public had an ask of $500K... five times as much as what could be a gigantic medical break through? Something seems fishy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-14-2015, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T17:43:30-07:00","id":709624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/700392-draco-a-potential-end-to-all-viral-disease-has-an-indigogo-campaign?p=700400#post700400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned the pharmaceutical companies they're trying to reach would take it and bury it. They make much more money treating symptoms than actually curing illnesses. Sick people are repeat customers, healthy ones are not.<br /> <br /> That said, very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, a couple of things:<br /> <br /> 1) We have antibiotics and antifungals now and pharmaceutical companies have not attempted to 'bury' them.<br /> 2) A broad spectrum antiviral would no more eliminate viral illness than antibiotics have eliminated bacterial illnesses. They would simply provide a standard treatment option.<br /> 3) Having a medication that\u2019s prescribed as often as antibotics are but for viral infections would increase the amount of money pharmaceutical companies get, not lower it.<br /> 4) There are a ton of medications out there that have nothing to do with infections.<br /> 5) You\u2019d still want to treat the symptoms. A cold is still going to give you a stuffy nose, sore throat, and fever, even if your doctor gives you an antiviral for it.<br /> <br /> If anything, people are likely to be less cautious about preventing and immunizing against illnesses if they believe there\u2019s a pill/injection they can take to fix things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/700392-draco-a-potential-end-to-all-viral-disease-has-an-indigogo-campaign?p=700447#post700447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds too good to be true. I am therefore doubtful</div> </div> </div> </div>The claim that it will 'end viral diseases' is farfetched. The claim that it might be an effective treatment for a wide-range of viral infections is not farfetched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 10-20-2015, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T03:45:38-07:00","id":710308,"title":"","content":"Plus there's the fact that they way modern capitalism works, treating sick people like repeat customers just means you're leaving an unexploited niche for the market of curing them, which some corporation will eventually leap upon with prices designed to be profitable and no competition, making a killing.<br /> <br /> That and how markets can be diverse enough that one can simultaneously cater to people with extended illnesses and ones that can be fixed in short order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T05:08:54-07:00","id":710380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/700392-draco-a-potential-end-to-all-viral-disease-has-an-indigogo-campaign?p=710308#post710308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus there's the fact that they way modern capitalism works, treating sick people like repeat customers just means you're leaving an unexploited niche for the market of curing them, which some corporation will eventually leap upon with prices designed to be profitable and no competition, making a killing.<br /> <br /> That and how markets can be diverse enough that one can simultaneously cater to people with extended illnesses and ones that can be fixed in short order.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a degree. Some sickness and aliments deal with such a small percentage of the population that research into treatments isn't viable or the process has been patented as is held by a patent troll/company who's rent seeking behavior nixes any profits gained by putting the drug into production. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T06:31:14-07:00","id":710459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/700392-draco-a-potential-end-to-all-viral-disease-has-an-indigogo-campaign?p=710380#post710380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some sickness and aliments deal with such a small percentage of the population that research into treatments isn't viable or the process has been patented as is held by a patent troll/company who's rent seeking behavior nixes any profits gained by putting the drug into production.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And there are other companies who issue those treatments basically for free as a humanitarian effort because the cost of producing such a small quantity is basically negligible, and other occasions in which governments implement measures to incentivize them to produce the drugs such as ten-year exclusivity guarantees.<br /> <br /> It's diverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{